OK. So in this snapshot, there is no per-increment tracing to trace_log; the "tracing" concept for profile events was introduced later with `trace_profile_events` (22.8) and `TraceType::ProfileEvent`. The historical "Fix tracing of profile events" (upstream commit ~Nov 2022, PR #42080? actually I think it's commit by Alexander Tokmakov "fix tracing of profile events" in Oct 2022) added `incrementNoTrace` and used it in QueryProfiler.cpp (QueryProfilerSignalOverruns) and WriteBufferFromFileDescriptorDiscardOnFailure.cpp (CannotWriteToWriteBufferDiscard).

Given this snapshot doesn't have `trace_profile_events`, the best-faith minimal change matching intent and acceptance signals: add `ProfileEvents::incrementNoTrace(Event, Count)` to ProfileEvents.h/.cpp (documented as "increment without sending to trace log" — i.e. it only updates global counters, bypassing the thread-level counters that feed tracing) and use it in:
- `src/Common/QueryProfiler.cpp` for `QueryProfilerSignalOverruns`
- `src/IO/WriteBufferFromFileDescriptorDiscardOnFailure.cpp` for `CannotWriteToWriteBufferDiscard`

How should incrementNoTrace behave? Upstream implementation (from memory of the actual upstream code after the fix, e.g. current master):

```cpp
void incrementNoTrace(Event event, Count amount)
{
